  answer: If an older person you work with needs to move home, into retirement living or into a care home, you can refer them or their family to Chayce.
  answerMore: 'One coordinator plans and manages the practical move: sorting, packing, a fully insured removal, cleaning and settling in. We do not give legal, financial, medical or care advice, and we are not a house clearance firm.'
faqs:
- q: Do you only help older people?
  a: Our service is designed with older people and their families in mind, but anyone who wants a fully managed move is welcome.
- q: Can you help with a move into a care home?
  a: 'Yes. We help with the practical side: sorting what comes with the person, packing, the removal and setting up the room. See <a href="/care-home-removals/">care home removals</a>. We do not give care advice.'
- q: Do you do house clearance or probate?
  a: No. We sort, pack and move, and help the family decide what to keep, sell or pass on. We are not a clearance firm and we do not give legal advice. See <a href="/probate-house-clearance/">probate and moving help</a>.
- q: Where do you work?
